To be precise: because the current code has **no database queries, no user input, no template rendering, no file I/O, and no deserialization**, the classic injection categories (SQLi, XSS, path traversal, command injection) **do not apply to the existing code**. The risk is that the missing scaffolding above makes it easy to introduce those vulnerabilities the moment the app grows. The recommendations above build the guardrails before they're needed.

