### Finding 10 — Server Binds to All Interfaces on a Fixed Port (OWASP A05: Security Misconfiguration) 🟢 Low

**Problem:** `app.listen(3000)` hardcodes the port and, more importantly, binds to `0.0.0.0` (all interfaces) by default. In a multi-interface environment this may expose the service unintentionally.

**Recommendation:**
```js
const PORT = parseInt(process.env.PORT ?? '3000', 10);
const HOST = process.env.HOST ?? '127.0.0.1'; // loopback only unless explicitly overridden

app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => {
  // Never log full config in production — it can expose environment details
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {
    console.log(`Server running on http://${HOST}:${PORT}`);
  }
});
```

