### 🟡 Issue 6 — No Structured Logging or Error Handling (A09)

There is no global error handler. Unhandled errors in Express will either crash the process or leak a full stack trace to the client (in development mode). Neither is acceptable in production.

**Recommendation:** Add a structured logger and a global error handler as the last middleware:
```js
const pino = require('pino');
const logger = pino({ level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info' });

// Attach logger to every request
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  req.log = logger.child({ requestId: crypto.randomUUID() });
  req.log.info({ method: req.method, url: req.url }, 'incoming request');
  next();
});

// Global error handler — MUST be defined last
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const status = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;
  // Log full error internally...
  req.log?.error({ err, status }, 'unhandled error');
  // ...but never send internals to the client
  res.status(status).json({
    error: status < 500 ? err.message : 'An unexpected error occurred',
  });
});
```

