### 🟡 Finding 8 — No Centralized Error Handler (OWASP A05)

**File:** `app.js` — entire file

**Problem:** There is no global error handling middleware. Unhandled errors in Express will return default stack traces to the client, leaking internal paths, dependency versions, and application structure.

**Fix:**

```js
// ✅ FIXED — place this AFTER all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log full error internally (use a proper logger like pino/winston)
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method,
  });

  // Return a generic message to the client — never leak stack traces
  const status = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;
  res.status(status).json({
    error: status < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred.',
  });
});

// Also handle unhandled promise rejections at the process level
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
  // Optionally: gracefully shut down
});
```

